60	/// head is already committed, so no header can change at this point. Nor does its JSON gain a
61	/// `retryable` key — that would add a field the OpenAI envelope shape (AC 3) does not have, on
62	/// this one frame only. Retryability is derivable anyway without either mechanism: `upstream-error`
63	/// is by construction the transient mid-stream case (the request already reached the upstream and
64	/// was streaming successfully before it failed), so a client that recognizes this code already
65	/// knows it may retry.
66	///
67	/// The frame STARTS with a blank line (SMA-635 spec §4.6). An upstream failure can fall inside a
68	/// record; without the blank line the frame would join that partial record and no SSE parser
69	/// could read it. After a clean record boundary the extra blank line is an empty record, which
70	/// dispatches nothing, so a client that reads a clean boundary sees no change.
71	pub(crate) const TERMINAL_SSE_ERROR: &str = "\n\ndata: {\"error\":{\"message\":\"upstream stream error\",\"type\":\"api_error\",\"param\":null,\"code\":\"upstream-error\"}}\n\n";
